# WordPress embed example

Use this snippet in a WordPress custom HTML block or within a shortcode plugin.

```html
<div id="solar-chatbot"></div>
<script src="https://yourdomain.com/chat-widget.js"></script>
<script>
  window.SolarChat.init({
    apiUrl: 'https://yourdomain.com',
    companyName: 'SunPeak Solar',
    containerId: 'solar-chatbot'
  });
</script>
```

If you prefer a floating button design, you can also wrap the script in a custom plugin and inject it into the footer of the WordPress site.

## Suggested WordPress plugin approach
- Create a custom plugin named `sunpeak-solar-chatbot`
- Enqueue the widget JS in the footer
- Add a div with id `solar-chatbot`
- Initialize the script after the div loads

This is a clean way to let the client insert the chatbot without editing theme files directly.

## Example plugin flow
```php
<?php
add_action('wp_footer', function () {
    echo '<div id="solar-chatbot"></div>';
    echo '<script src="https://yourdomain.com/chat-widget.js"></script>';
    echo "<script>window.SolarChat.init({ apiUrl: 'https://yourdomain.com', companyName: 'SunPeak Solar', containerId: 'solar-chatbot' });</script>";
});
```
